Title: Bar Attendant

Company: MKS Trading WA Pty Ltd

Location: Roebuck WA 6725

Salary: $70,000 to $80,000

Job Type: Full-Time


MKS Trading WA Pty Ltd operates Roebuck Plains Roadhouse, a regional hospitality and accommodation business operating in Roebuck, Western Australia, servicing highway travellers, tourists, and local customers. The business operates a fast-paced roadhouse style environment providing motel accommodation, food and beverage services, and general customer services. The business is seeking experienced and customer-focused Bar Attendant to join our hospitality team on a full-time basis.

Key Responsibilities:

• Prepare and serve a range of alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages to customers;

• Provide friendly and efficient bar service, including counter and table service;

• Operate point of sale systems and process customer payments accurately;

• Maintain bar presentation, cleanliness and hygiene standards;

• Assist with monitoring beverage supplies, replenishment of stock and stock control activities;

• Ensure responsible service of alcohol practices are followed, including checking customer identification where required;

• Respond to customer enquiries and provide professional customer service;

• Support front of house operations and work effectively with other hospitality team members;

• Assist with opening and closing duties, including preparation, cleaning and restocking of the bar area;

• Follow workplace health and safety, food safety and venue procedures.

Requirements:

• Minimum 12 months' relevant experience as a Bar Attendant, Bartender or in a similar hospitality role;

• Current Responsible Service of Alcohol (RSA) certificate;

• Excellent customer service and communication skills;

• Experience operating a point of sale (POS) system and handling cash transactions;

• Ability to work efficiently in a busy hospitality environment;

• Availability to work a rotating roster, including evenings, weekends and public holidays.

Employment Conditions:

• Full-time position;

• Competitive salary plus superannuation;

• Rotating roster, including weekends and public holidays;

• Opportunity to work in a well-established regional hospitality business.

How to Apply: Interested candidates should submit a resume and cover letter outlining their relevant experience and suitability for the role.

Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.

Salary: $70,000 to $80,000 per year excluding superannuation
